EastSun: "你屬性裡面的事件我希望可以像WPF一樣有很多表格事件，如果有設定事件上面就會顯示是
什麼函式，並且雙擊兩下可以跑到對應CODE，如果沒有設定就會自動新增相關設定". He chose the C++
port tree for new handlers.
- lib/vclevents.js: BCB6's (VCL 6) published events per class (TForm,
  TButton, TSpeedButton, TLabel, TEdit, TComboBox, TPageControl, TTimer,
  grids ...; an unknown class = TControl's), plus the ones the .dfm assigns;
  BCB6's handler names (spbSaveClick, FormShow), the VCL signatures, and
  which ones WS form.event carries (OnClick = click, OnChange = change).
- the 事件 section is the whole list: the handler of a set one (the .dfm's,
  or one the port has by BCB6's name, or the server table's) and four marks:
  網頁 (the page's *_ev.js CTLS list sends it), 伺服器 (the generated
  form.event tables in FileRW / JsonBridge have the row), C++, BCB6; the
  places found are listed under a set one.
- a double-click: a set one -> its code (as before); an empty one -> like
  BCB6: the declaration in the form's class (forms/f*.h, after its last
  event handler, same indentation and line ends) and an empty body at the end
  of forms/f*.cpp -- one edit, nothing saved -- then the .cpp opens at it.
  A name already declared (a GATE on purpose) is not added twice.
  The page's CTLS entry and the server's event table are said, not written:
  they are the event-porting pipeline's (tools/editlist, gen_editlist.py,
  which take golden handlers only) -- RegisterPageEvents keeps ONE table per
  page, so a second hand-written registration would replace the generated one.
- lib/cppstub.js: the class body with comments / strings / char literals
  skipped, where the declaration goes, the body text.

Tests (all 4 layers pass: lib 149, smoke 153, real VS Code 139): lib
(the lists, names, signatures; the stub on the real forms/fHotPlate.h / .cpp
read in memory: only the insertions differ), smoke (spbSave's grid, OnMouseUp
created with its VCL signature, nothing on disk, a second double-click opens
it), panels (the grid posts eventGrid, the places under OnClick), real VS Code
(OnDblClick -> TfHotPlate::spbSaveDblClick in fHotPlate.h / .cpp, reverted,
the files on disk unchanged).

